---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Contribute">
  <main class="wrap narrow contribute-page">
    <header class="page-header contribute-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Help improve the catalog</p>
      <h1>Contribute</h1>
      <p class="muted contribute-intro">Help keep this catalog concrete, current, and useful.</p>

      <div class="contribute-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/nickmvincent/data-licenses/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open an issue</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/nickmvincent/data-licenses/compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open a PR</a>
        <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="https://nickmvincent.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact Nick</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="box section">
      <h2>Quick checklist</h2>
      <ul class="contribute-checklist">
        <li>Confirm the initiative has a clear AI data rights angle, not just general anti-AI security or abstract research.</li>
        <li>Include one canonical website and at least one dated public source for any factual update.</li>
        <li>Keep summaries short, neutral, and specific about what actually ships or changed.</li>
        <li>If you add a user, data, or payment metric, add matching <code>metricEvidence</code> sources too.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="box section">
      <h2>What we're capturing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Initiatives that shape AI data flows via preference signals, licenses/terms, collectives, data market platforms, technical controls, certification, or new infrastructures.</li>
        <li>Concrete implementation details, canonical websites, and dated evidence links for updates or adoption.</li>
        <li>Practical metadata: live or wip status, pipeline stages, data types, jurisdictions, and adoption signals (users/data/money).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="box section">
      <h2>What's not in scope (for now)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>General-purpose anti-AI cybersecurity without a clear data rights angle.</li>
        <li>Pure research concepts without a public artifact or path to adoption.</li>
        <li>Content provenance-only work unless it directly informs data licensing or preferences.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="box section">
      <h2>How to contribute</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Suggest a new initiative or update an existing one, ideally with a canonical site and dated evidence links.</li>
        <li>Use the issue tracker when you want to flag a lead or discuss scope before writing content.</li>
        <li>Open a PR when you already have the source-backed wording and metadata ready to review.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted small">Developers can add or update a markdown file under <code>content/initiatives/</code>. Each entry should have one canonical <code>website</code>, a <code>status</code> of <code>live</code> or <code>wip</code>, <code>visibility: public</code>, <code>type: data_license_initiative</code>, and optional dated <code>evidenceLinks</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="box section">
      <h2>Research method</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Read the <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> before proposing updates. It explains how we decide what counts as a real update and how metrics are grounded.</li>
        <li>AI-assisted first passes are welcome, but every suggested <code>evidenceLinks</code>, <code>usersCount</code>, <code>dataVolume</code>, or <code>moneyVolume</code> value should come with a clickable source and date. If you add a metric, also add matching <code>metricEvidence</code>.</li>
        <li>You can start from the public <a href="/prompts/find-updates.txt">research prompt</a>, the current <a href="/data/initiatives.json">catalog JSON</a>, and the curation backlog at <a href="/data/curation.json">/data/curation.json</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .contribute-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .contribute-hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .contribute-intro {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .contribute-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .contribute-checklist {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .contribute-actions .btn {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
